From 5b36ef23af2ca0ba09f423025651aed5f6eedb34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:50:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Implement V2 VM context and Merkle proof opcodes

Implement authenticated transaction, input, resolved-coin, output, invocation, and lock introspection alongside sorted and indexed four-algorithm Merkle folds. Require exact operand widths, proof framing and bounds, and fail closed on mint coin reads and invalid indices.

Charge bounded proof steps using the explicit caller schedule, add independent Python Merkle vectors and native context/rejection cases, and refresh assigned-opcode coverage. This remains a review candidate without frozen network cost coefficients.
